25,2,1,talk,May,,"It seems some old ideas actually worked, specifically a late-evening trial, but some infrastructure priorities from a decade ago didn't stick.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,We are in trouble. The late-turn pool is thin and roadway crews are well below establishment. We can't just add more shifts.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Midori,,"Interestingly, the mid-city crowds aren't the main issue. The real time-loss is happening during connections, not during the actual transit.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"I've found that working in old stations is risky due to unrecorded voids, and getting different operators to agree on data is a nightmare.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Our ticketing fees are ballooning, and while we have some ring-fenced construction money, our operating subsidies are being trimmed.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, if the crews are that short, any plan requiring more manpower is a non-starter regardless of historical success.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Exactly. Unless the plan uses existing maintenance capacity, which I did notice is available for lifts and escalators.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Jonathan, if the operating subsidy is shrinking, we should focus on the most efficient time-saves for passengers.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@May, the ""hidden"" physical risks in the old shells make me very nervous about any major structural rework.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, that matches my fear of contingency costs. We need something that doesn't create a financial black hole.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,May,,"@Midori, if the issue is connections, perhaps a simplified system would help more than just adding lanes.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,I'm leaning away from anything that adds to the late-night burden on our exhausted crews.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, that's a fair point. We should look for a solution that doesn't rely on the late-turn pool.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Shizue,,I'm glad to hear the maintenance contract for lifts has spare capacity. That's a rare bit of good news.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,We must avoid any plan that increases our reliance on expensive external ticketing contractors.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
