50,3,1,talk,May,,"Looking at the candidates, the Integrated Fare Platform (A) aligns with the successful contactless pilot I found.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,I must oppose the Night Service Extension (D). Our rosters are already depleted; we cannot sustain more late shifts.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Midori,,The Crosstown Bus Corridor (B) seems unnecessary if the crowd counts are stable and the issue is actually connections.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Station Access Upgrades (C) sound risky due to the pre-war shells, but the maintenance crew capacity is a plus.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Plan A looks expensive regarding contractors, but Plan C could be a budget disaster if those voids are found.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,May,,"@Shizue, the accessibility records show some of those rebuilds actually finished on time. It's not all risk.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, I still think Plan C is the safest for staffing since the lift maintenance contract has spare capacity.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Jonathan, if we want to fix connections, Plan A's single account system is the most logical step for the passenger.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, but Plan A requires the ferry and rail offices to agree, and my research says they never do.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,Shizue is right. The inter-agency friction makes Plan A a high-risk administrative failure.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,May,,"If A is a bureaucratic mess and D is a staffing nightmare, we are left with B and C.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"B requires roadway crews, who are understaffed. C uses the lift crews, who have capacity. C is the logical choice.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Midori,,"I can support C. While it's not a direct fix for connection timing, it improves the overall flow.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"I'm still worried about the shells, but compared to the other options, it's the most feasible.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"If the capital ledger has ring-fenced construction funds, Plan C is the most fiscally responsible use of that specific pot.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,4,talk,May,,I agree. Let's go with the Station Access Upgrades.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,Agreed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,4,talk,Midori,,Agreed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,4,talk,Shizue,,Agreed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,Agreed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
